{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.SMul","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Lemmas"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hooks_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hooks_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L480-L500","doc":"**The `n` hooks are linearly independent** — the `≥ n` half of `rank = n`.\n\nFunctional `m` is evaluation at `z_{m+1}`; hook `k` vanishes there iff `m+1 ≤ k` iff `m < k`,\nand hook `m` is nonzero there. Uniform in `m` — the last hook needs no special case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookNum_eval_legRoot_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookNum_eval_legRoot_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L465-L477","doc":"Hook `(n−k,1^k)` is NONZERO at leg root `z_m` when `k < m`: no leg factor `i ≤ k` is the\n`m`-th, and no arm factor vanishes there. The `≠ 0` hypotheses are the genericity conditions on\n`q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookNum_eval_legRoot_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookNum_eval_legRoot_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L454-L462","doc":"Hook `(n−k,1^k)` vanishes at leg root `z_m` for `1 ≤ m ≤ k`: the `m`-th leg factor is in the\nproduct. This is the row cap in polynomial form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookNum","kind":"def","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L447-L451","doc":"Numerator of the hook `(n−k, 1^k)`: one diagonal cell (constant), `n−k−1` arm cells, `k`\nleg cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.legFactor_eval_legRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.legFactor_eval_legRoot","kind":"theorem","line":437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L437-L444","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.legRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.legRoot","kind":"def","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L431-L434","doc":"The root of the `i`-th leg factor, `z_i = q^{2i}(q²−1)/(q(q^{2i}−1))` — which is the Ocneanu\nfamily parameter `q^i/[i]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.legFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.legFactor","kind":"def","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L427-L429","doc":"Leg cell `(i,0)`, `i ≥ 1`: numerator factor `q^{2i}(q²−1) − q(q^{2i}−1)·z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.armFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.armFactor","kind":"def","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L422-L424","doc":"Arm cell `(0,j)`, `j ≥ 1`: numerator factor `(q²−1) + q(q^{2j}−1)·z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.linearIndependent_of_triangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.linearIndependent_of_triangular","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L393-L419","doc":"**Triangular independence** (generic). If functionals `φ m` satisfy `φ m (f k) = 0` for\n`m < k` and `φ m (f m) ≠ 0`, then `f` is linearly independent: apply `φ 0` to a vanishing\ncombination to isolate `c 0`, then `φ 1`, and so on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuFamily_finrank_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuFamily_finrank_le","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L347-L367","doc":"**The Ocneanu family at level `n` spans at most `n` dimensions**, against the `p(n)` dimensions\nof the full space of trace functionals on `H_n(q)`.\n\nThis is the `≤` half of the measured `rank = n`; equality is **not** proved (see\n`markov_trace_family_rank_probe.py`, exact at `n = 2..6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuOffDiag_card_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuOffDiag_card_lt","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L338-L344","doc":"Off-diagonal cells are strictly fewer than all cells, because `(0,0)` is diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_span_eval_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_span_eval_le","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L317-L336","doc":"**The family spans at most `d+1` dimensions.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.eval_mem_span_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.eval_mem_span_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L299-L314","doc":"A family of polynomials of degree `≤ d`, evaluated at `z`, lies in the span of the `d+1`\ncoefficient vectors — for **every** `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumPoly_natDegree_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumPoly_natDegree_le","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L266-L282","doc":"**The degree bound.** The numerator's degree in `z` is at most the number of cells **off** the\ndiagonal — equivalently `|μ| − d(μ)`, since the diagonal cells contribute constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_natDegree_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_natDegree_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L258-L263","doc":"A cell factor is linear in `z`, hence of degree at most one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumPoly_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumPoly_eval","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L247-L255","doc":"`ocneanuNumPoly` really is the numerator: evaluating at `z` returns it. Without this the degree\nbound below would be a statement about a free-standing polynomial rather than about the weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumPoly","kind":"def","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L240-L244","doc":"The Ocneanu numerator as a polynomial in the Markov parameter `z`, with the affine form of\n`ocneanuNumFactor_affine` as its per-cell factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.mem_cells_diag_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.mem_cells_diag_zero","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L214-L219","doc":"**Every non-empty diagram has a diagonal cell**, namely `(0,0)`. So `d(μ) ≥ 1` and the top\n`z`-power `z^{|μ|}` always dies — the naive degree bound from `|μ|` affine factors is never\nattained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNum_diagonal_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNum_diagonal_split","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L195-L212","doc":"**The `z`-dependence of the numerator is confined to the off-diagonal cells.**\n\nThe product splits into a `z`-free part over the diagonal cells and a part over the off-diagonal\ncells, each factor there affine in `z` with a nonzero-in-general coefficient. The number of factors\nthat can carry `z` is therefore `|μ| − d(μ)`, `d(μ)` the count of diagonal cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_diagonal_z_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_diagonal_z_free","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L189-L193","doc":"**A diagonal cell contributes no `z`.** At `i = j` the two `z` terms cancel identically, so the\nfactor is the constant `q^{2i}(q² − 1)`. Unconditional: no hypothesis on `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_affine","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L183-L187","doc":"**The cell numerator factor is affine in `z`**, with `z`-coefficient `q^{2j+1} − q^{2i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_of_three_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_of_three_rows","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L137-L153","doc":"**At the convention-D Markov parameter `z = q³/(q²+1)`, every partition with three or more rows\nhas weight zero.**\n\nThe hypothesis `0 < μ.rowLen 2` says the third row is nonempty, i.e. `μ` has at least three rows;\nequivalently `(2,0) ∈ μ`, a cell of content `−2`, whose numerator factor vanishes at this `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_eq_zero_of_content_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_eq_zero_of_content_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L127-L135","doc":"The numerator factor of a cell of content `−2` vanishes at `z = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L86-L93","doc":"**The Ocneanu/Markov weight of a Young diagram**, one closed form for every `n`.\n\n`w_μ(q,z) = ∏_{(i,j) ∈ μ} (q^{2i}(q² − 1 − qz) + q^{2j+1} z) / ∏_{(i,j) ∈ μ} (q^{2h(i,j)} − 1)`.\n\nSee the module docstring for how this was derived and for what is *not* proved about it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookLength","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeight.lean#L80-L84","doc":"Hook length of the cell `c` in the Young diagram `μ`: arm (cells weakly to the right of `c` in\nits row, `c` included) plus leg (cells strictly below `c` in its column). ","signatureChunk":0}]}